      "writtenOn": "2021-08-30T01:40:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It sounds likes this only read 512 bytes. But code says it reads [UUID + u64(LE)] from the location(offset). Can you clarify the comment?\n\nPartitionHeader struct consists of \"uuid + offset + size\" while its serialization consists of \"uuid + size\". How about making it 1:1? It would be easier to read if serialization resembles the struct itself. The parameter \u0027header_offset\u0027 can be verified against the read value of offset.\n\nAdditionally, I\u0027d like to put \"PartitionHeader\" marker as well (just like ZIP file\u0027s local header) so that we can be sure if we\u0027re reading PartitionHeader, not a random block of memory.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 176,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "4b535374648e0fb28d0510b63fcbc5071f44bf5d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "30c45477_89abd80a",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/instance.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 176,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-30T03:10:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. s/block/header/\n\nRemoved header_offset from PartitionHeader. Instead, locate_microdroid_header returns (PartitionHeader, PartitionOffset).\n\nPutting a magic string inside a partition header doesn\u0027t give better protection because the partition header is used as additionally authenticated data (AAD) when encrypting/decrypting the payload, which means that an incorrect header will anyway fail the decryption.",
      "parentUuid": "3de29570_857e11a7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 176,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "4b535374648e0fb28d0510b63fcbc5071f44bf5d",
